  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper proposes a hybrid variational quantum machine learning classifier using amplitude encoding and PQCs, reporting a mean classification accuracy of 96.42% versus ~91% for classical models across 10 trials. Scalability experiments up to 10,000 samples report quantum runtime of 58.1 s versus 140.8 s classical and fidelity improvement from 0.856 to 0.927 using ZNE/QEM, but experiments use small (≤16‑qubit) simulated NISQ circuits and unspecified datasets.",
